  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 809.04 Reclamation Facility Requirements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 809.04 Reclamation Facility Requirements. An owner or operator of a facility at which spent lead-acid batteries are reclaimed other than through regeneration shall:\n\n(a) Comply with Env-Hw 400, Env-Hw 502, and the applicable requirements of Env-Hw 1200; and\n\n(b) If spent lead-acid batteries are stored at the facility prior to reclamation, the owner or operator shall be subject to the:\n\n(1) Storage facility permit requirements specified in Env-Hw 300; and\n\n(2) Facility requirements specified in Env-Hw 700, except for:\n\na. The waste analysis requirements of Env-Hw 707.03(a)(2) and Env-Hw 708.02(a)(2); and\n\nb. The manifest requirements of Env-Hw 703.\n\nSource. #5053, eff 1-24-91; ss by #5886, eff 8-26-94; ss by #7333, eff 8-1-00; ss by #7578, eff 10-13-01; ss by #9367, eff 1-28-09; amd by #10205, eff 10-19-12; ss by #12350, eff 8-14-17; ss by #12922, eff 11-23-19; ss by #14526, eff 2-28-26, EXPIRES: 2-28-36",
